We have,
$x^2-4 x+4 y^2=12x^2-4 x+4 y^2=12\begin{array}{ll}\Rightarrow & (x-2)^2+4(y-0)^2=8 \\ \Rightarrow & \frac{(x-2)^2}{(2 \sqrt{2})^2}+\frac{(y-0)^2}{(\sqrt{2})}=1\end{array}
which is an ellipse whose major and minor axes are $2 a=2 \sqrt{2}$ and $2 b=\sqrt{2}$ repectively.
$\therefore$ Its eccentricity $\theta$ is given by
$\begin{aligned} e & =\sqrt{1-\frac{b^2}{a^2}} \\ & =\sqrt{1-\frac{2}{8}}=\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\end{aligned}
